# Routing and Navigation Rules

## 🗺️ Routing Architecture

### Route Structure

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Route organization in App.tsx
<Routes>
  <Route element={<Layout />}>
    <Route path={ROUTE.HOME} element={<Home />} />
    <Route path={ROUTE.CALENDAR} element={<Calendar />} />

    {/* Nested routes */}
    <Route path={ROUTE.COMMUNITY.BASE} element={<Community />}>
      <Route path={ROUTE.COMMUNITY.LIST} element={<CommunityList />} />
      <Route path={ROUTE.COMMUNITY.WRITE} element={<CommunityWrite />} />
      <Route path={ROUTE.COMMUNITY.DETAIL} element={<ArticleDetail />} />
    </Route>

    {/* Admin routes */}
    <Route path={ROUTE.ADMIN.BASE} element={<Admin />}>
      <Route path={ROUTE.ADMIN.APPROVAL} element={<Approval />} />
      <Route path={ROUTE.ADMIN.INFO} element={<MemberInfo />} />
    </Route>
  </Route>
</Routes>
```

### MUST FOLLOW Rules

✅ **ALWAYS** use React Router DOM for navigation
✅ **ALWAYS** define routes in constants file
✅ **ALWAYS** use nested routes for related pages
✅ **ALWAYS** implement proper route protection
✅ **ALWAYS** handle 404 routes with NotFound component
✅ **ALWAYS** use proper route parameters
✅ **ALWAYS** implement loading states for route transitions

### NEVER DO Rules

❌ **NEVER** use window.location for navigation
❌ **NEVER** hardcode route paths in components
❌ **NEVER** forget to handle route parameters
❌ **NEVER** create routes without proper protection
❌ **NEVER** forget to implement 404 handling
❌ **NEVER** use anchor tags for internal navigation

### Route Constants

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Route constants structure
const ROUTE = Object.freeze({
  HOME: "/",
  CALENDAR: "/calendar",
  COMMUNITY: {
    BASE: "/community",
    LIST: "",
    WRITE: "write",
    UPDATE: "update",
    DETAIL: ":id",
    NOT_FOUND: "404-not-found",
  },
  ADMIN: {
    BASE: "/admin",
    APPROVAL: "approval",
